-- A LIST OF FINDINGS BETWEEN ITS SUMMARY: a library
-- (`use("cookbook:roc/summed.shale")`) for the Roc recipes that print a
-- list no tree bounds. Each such recipe says `output_bytes=4000000` in its
-- `-- budget:` line, since 64 KiB unset holds a few hundred findings, and
-- prints its summary both first and last: first, so a run the output
-- budget stops still says its totals; last, because a verify reads a
-- recipe's last line (roc-chat's tools/verify_hunts.shale).

-- `summary`, then each line of `found`, then `summary` again (once, when
-- `found` is empty).
function print_summed(summary, found)
  print(summary)
  if #found == 0 then return nil end
  for l in found do print(l) end
  print(summary)
  return nil
end
